WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.275
A portable document can contain several diagrams.

00:00:04.395 --> 00:00:13.170
Connected WBS and Gantt diagrams answer different
questions about the same work: what belongs in the
project, and when that work happens.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:21.065
In this lesson we create the schedule from a breakdown,
navigate between members, inspect linked details, and save
the document.

00:00:21.185 --> 00:00:27.985
Keep a distinction between a separate open tab and a
diagram that belongs to the same portable document.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.625
Begin with the customer portal breakdown.

00:00:34.745 --> 00:00:38.945
Open Plan and choose Create Gantt chart from WBS.

00:00:39.065 --> 00:00:43.640
Review the document name and project start date before
creating it.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:50.035
The application creates a schedule and retains the WBS as
a member of the same document.

00:00:50.155 --> 00:00:56.305
This is a useful starting point, but a work breakdown does
not supply every scheduling decision.

00:00:56.425 --> 00:01:03.850
Review task duration, ordering, resources and dependencies
before treating the generated schedule as a commitment.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:11.692
The document navigator lists the diagrams that belong
together.

00:01:11.812 --> 00:01:17.562
Select the WBS member to review structure, then the Gantt
member to review the schedule.

00:01:17.682 --> 00:01:22.407
These are different sources, even though the linked work
connects their meaning.

00:01:22.527 --> 00:01:26.002
Changing the selected diagram is navigation.

00:01:26.122 --> 00:01:30.047
It does not duplicate the work or create another schedule.

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:36.242
Keep the navigator visible while learning the document so
you can recognize which member you are editing.

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:43.617
Return to the WBS and select a work item.

00:01:43.737 --> 00:01:49.287
Its inspector provides the supported work details and
linked Gantt task control.

00:01:49.407 --> 00:01:56.682
Follow a link when you want to inspect the corresponding
schedule item, and check the destination before editing
dates.

00:01:56.802 --> 00:02:02.527
A relationship between diagrams does not mean every line
of their source is identical.

00:02:02.647 --> 00:02:06.522
Structure and schedule retain their own responsibilities.

00:02:06.642 --> 00:02:14.967
Review shared details deliberately, and avoid creating an
unrelated duplicate task simply because you cannot see the
other member.

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:22.717
As a project grows, compare the work represented on each
side.

00:02:22.837 --> 00:02:26.962
A new WBS item may still need a scheduled task.

00:02:27.082 --> 00:02:35.682
The Plan command can add missing WBS tasks to the linked
Gantt chart, while existing links help avoid duplicating
covered work.

00:02:35.802 --> 00:02:43.327
Review the coverage and deletion choices rather than
assuming that removing a shape should remove every related
object.

00:02:43.447 --> 00:02:50.522
Return to the breakdown and verify that the missing-task
count is zero; the existing work is not duplicated.

00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:59.183
Delete Requirements from the WBS in a disposable connected
copy.

00:02:59.303 --> 00:03:05.128
The linked-work dialog explains which Gantt task is
affected and offers a deliberate choice.

00:03:05.248 --> 00:03:08.973
Choose Keep Gantt tasks, then inspect both members.

00:03:09.093 --> 00:03:15.293
Requirements is gone from the breakdown, while its
scheduled task remains with its dates and assignments.

00:03:15.413 --> 00:03:22.463
Review the resulting coverage rather than assuming a
deletion on one side must remove useful work everywhere.

00:03:25.967 --> 00:03:33.042
Repeat the small deletion in a fresh connected practice
copy, but this time choose Delete in both diagrams.

00:03:33.162 --> 00:03:38.012
Check that Requirements is removed from the WBS and from
the schedule.

00:03:38.132 --> 00:03:45.107
This option has a wider effect than keeping the
counterpart, so inspect the affected work before accepting
it.

00:03:45.227 --> 00:03:52.277
Use separate disposable copies to learn the two outcomes,
and preserve a saved project before a real cleanup.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.775
New work can also begin in the schedule.

00:03:58.895 --> 00:04:05.695
Add Training review as a Gantt task, then inspect the
command for missing Gantt work in the linked WBS.

00:04:05.815 --> 00:04:08.990
Add the counterpart and inspect the breakdown.

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:15.260
Review its placement and meaning before treating the
generated node as a finished scope decision.

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:21.455
Coverage helps find missing counterparts; it does not
decide how you should organize the project.

00:04:24.967 --> 00:04:30.692
Create an unlinked Acceptance slot in the schedule of this
disposable connected project.

00:04:30.812 --> 00:04:35.312
Add Acceptance review independently to the work breakdown
structure.

00:04:35.432 --> 00:04:40.807
Select that node and choose the existing Acceptance slot
as its linked Gantt task.

00:04:40.927 --> 00:04:47.452
Open the linked task to verify that counterpart navigation
reaches the intended scheduled item.

00:04:47.572 --> 00:04:52.022
Check that coverage reports no unlinked items after the
repair.

00:04:52.142 --> 00:04:59.542
Save the portable document with its repaired mapping;
linking existing work should not create a second scheduled
task.

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:07.067
Save the containing document as a portable pumlu file.

00:05:07.187 --> 00:05:15.312
The document holds its member diagrams and their links, so
it is the appropriate handover when another person needs
the connected project.

00:05:15.432 --> 00:05:22.882
Exporting one member as plain Plant UML source serves a
different purpose and does not replace the whole document.

00:05:23.002 --> 00:05:28.677
Reopen the saved practice document and verify that both
members remain available.

00:05:28.797 --> 00:05:35.247
Keep an untouched practice copy before experimenting with
imports, member removal or link changes.

00:05:38.767 --> 00:05:42.717
Import the plain Sequence source into the connected
document.

00:05:42.837 --> 00:05:47.587
Check the new member and its source before renaming it
Portal request flow.

00:05:47.707 --> 00:05:55.307
A member name helps people navigate the document, while
aliases inside that diagram identify its modeled objects.

00:05:55.427 --> 00:06:02.827
Save the portable document after checking the imported
member alongside the existing WBS and Gantt views.

00:06:02.947 --> 00:06:10.072
Importing a plain source diagram does not automatically
create semantic object links to the existing members.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:17.950
A document member can also be removed from the containing
project.

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:26.970
Import the disposable Sequence example, inspect the three
members, then choose Delete for that imported diagram and
read the confirmation.

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:31.540
Verify that the WBS and Gantt members remain available.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:39.585
This is a document member operation, distinct from
deleting a linked WBS work item or its scheduled
counterpart.

00:06:39.705 --> 00:06:47.255
Keep a saved copy before reorganizing a real project, and
check the intended member name before accepting removal.

00:06:50.767 --> 00:06:55.867
A document can also record object connections across
different diagram types.

00:06:55.987 --> 00:07:04.662
Import the request Sequence diagram and connect the
scheduled Backend work to its API participant using the
compatible link controls.

00:07:04.782 --> 00:07:12.207
The link labeled implements records this connection in the
document; the diagram sources retain their existing
arrows.

00:07:12.327 --> 00:07:17.727
Inspect the connection and its resolved endpoints, then
save the portable document.

00:07:17.847 --> 00:07:25.822
Keep these object connections distinct from the WBS to
Gantt scheduling counterparts and from an external web
link.

00:07:29.333 --> 00:07:33.558
Pause and create a connected document from the practice
breakdown.

00:07:33.678 --> 00:07:38.253
Navigate to both members and identify the corresponding
work.

00:07:38.373 --> 00:07:43.048
Add a missing work item, inspect coverage, and schedule it
deliberately.

00:07:43.168 --> 00:07:46.243
Rename a member so its purpose is clear.

00:07:46.363 --> 00:07:52.138
Save a portable copy, reopen it, and check that the
members and links remain available.

00:07:52.258 --> 00:08:00.258
Success means you can distinguish separate files from
members of a connected document and explain both the
structure and the schedule.

00:08:03.767 --> 00:08:08.542
A connected document combines distinct diagrams with
explicit links.

00:08:08.662 --> 00:08:12.937
Use WBS to organize work and Gantt to schedule it.

00:08:13.057 --> 00:08:21.957
Inspect coverage when either side changes, review deletion
consequences, and save the portable document when handing
over the full project.

00:08:22.077 --> 00:08:30.077
In the next group of lessons, the same habit of checking
identity and relationships will help you maintain the
software models as well.
